// A function from another file is called by that file's name. Called bare, the error
// names the line of the call, in the file it is in (modules/bare_call.nxa, line 3).
// It used to name no line at all.
#include <std/io>
#include "../modules/bare_call.nxa"
fn hello(): void { io.println("hi"); }
fn main() { bare_call.shout(); }
